e around x≈1090): three up-and-back groups, each a step higher than the last: E5 F5 E5, F5 G5 F5, G5 A5 G5. This is bar 25. The forte marking is not visible.\n\nThird bar (to the barline around x≈1650): the line climbs above the staff with ledger lines, A5 C6 Bb5. Then it falls step by step: A5 G5 F5, then E5 D5 C5. This is bar 26.\n\nFourth stretch: a small grace eighth (E5), then a falling group D5 C5 Bb4, then one quarter note around A4 at the right edge. This is the start of bar 27. The copy shows only the top note of the A4+F4 chord. The G4+C4 quarter and the end of the bar are missing, so the line stops partway through bar 27 and the next line finishes it.\n\nNothing contradicts the edition's pitches or rhythm.","right":true,"insights":"The line was easy to match because the triplet shapes are so distinctive: rising, then up-and-back, then a climb and a run down. The one bar that could be confused is 23, and its last group rises, which rules it out. The cut-off at the right edge, where only one quarter of bar 27 shows, was the only uncertain part. A slightly wider crop, or the start of the next line, would have confirmed where bar 27 ends."},"ttft_ms":14071,"type":"result","duration_ms":37331,"uuid":"c269515f-9f07-4771-a5b3-5d3888979ff8","ttft_stream_ms":1614,"time_to_request_ms":377,"first_content_frame_ms":1614,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":3156,"cacheReadInputTokens":1046,"cacheCreationInputTokens":11309,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.15381720000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2443,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":11309,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
